# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Node.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Local staging the installer writes; never part of the source tree.
.install/
*.log

# Verification residue (a suite that throws mid-run can leave these behind).
# /%SystemDrive%/ is an unexpanded cmd-style %VAR% one: something ran with this
# repo as its CWD and built the Windows chain under a literal folder name. Git
# cannot even report it while the tree holds no files, so the rule is what keeps
# it visible to a future cleanup. The writer is unidentified.
/tmp-probe/
/%SystemDrive%/
_debug-*.mjs

# Bytecode cache from py_compile on the shipped bridge source. Hygiene only:
# "files" in package.json whitelists all of lib/, and npm cannot exclude a
# files-included path through .gitignore — scripts.prepack is what keeps the
# cache out of the tarball. This rule keeps it out of git, nothing more.
lib/wsl/__pycache__/

# Release artifacts. `npm pack` output is reproducible from this tree and is
# never part of it — and a stale one is worse than noise: an older tarball can be
# a build that cannot load at all, sitting there installable.
*.tgz
